OBS --> API : validate V1 authorized facts only
API --> DOMAIN : compose detached bounded batch
API --> WIRE : delegate public V1 decoding
OLD --> WIRE : delegate unchanged shared bytes/errors
DOMAIN --> INTENTS : authorized maps + unknown masks
DOMAIN --> ORDER : structural coordinates only
DOMAIN --> PROMOTION : earlier prefix; authored coordinates retained
DOMAIN --> RESERVATION : immutable append-time anchors
DOMAIN --> TRAVERSE : canonically ordered intents
TRAVERSE --> WIRE : canonical V1 action-array bytes
TRAVERSE --> SHA : synchronous digest; compare raw bytes on collision
TRAVERSE --> BATCH : one funding pool per unique queue
NATIVE ..> INTENTS : shared pure calculations; preserve native permission
NATIVE ..> ORDER : actual rewrite still depends on native state
BATCH ..> ADMISSION : selected queue only; never a generator dependency

note right of PROMOTION
Promotion choices describe a possible Marine
landing, not a promise that native rules will
move or preserve the actor. Earlier B intents
can require five choices while authored
coordinates stay unchanged.
end note

note right of RESERVATION
Mine reservations record each valid intent at
append time, even if its actor may later die.
Potential removals do not release capacity,
and later C intents cannot shift an earlier
reservation or refund its reserved anchor.
end note

note bottom of TRAVERSE
512 candidates including pass.
2048 attempts; at most four actions.
end note

